# TurnKey CRM

TurnKey is a field-service CRM for pressure-washing businesses.

## Architecture

- The frontend is plain HTML, JavaScript and CSS with no frontend build step.
- `index.html` is the staff workspace; `booking.html` and `quote.html` are public.
- Frontend modules, shared engines and CSS live at the repository root.
- New UI goes in its own module, not `index.html`.
- `backend/` is the Express backend for integrations and secret-bearing work.
- Supabase provides Postgres, Auth, Storage and RLS.
- `supabase/migrations/` is the source of truth for database schema changes.
- Netlify serves static files. `scripts/build-static.js` prepares assets and
  `scripts/generate-config.js` generates `window.TURNKEY_CONFIG` in `config.js`.

## Shared logic and security

- Reuse `pricing-engine.js`, `cost-engine.js` and `sales-engine.js`.
- Public pricing must never include internal costs or margins.
- Escape every interpolated value from DB or user data before inserting HTML,
  including attributes; use local escaping helpers or `textContent`.
- Preserve `TK_POLICIES.renderPolicyHtml` output as policy HTML.
- Never expose service-role keys or backend secrets in frontend code or commits.
- Every new table needs RLS and explicit policies for business isolation.
- Add schema changes as new migrations; do not use legacy SQL as the schema.

## Working conventions

- Preserve existing behavior outside the request and match nearby patterns.
- Use scoped searches with up to 30 lines of context for `index.html` and files
  over 400 lines; never read those files whole.
- Other workers may share this checkout; stage only your own task files.
- Honor local-only instructions: no push, PR or remote service changes.
- Frontend checks: `node --test tests/*.test.cjs`.
- Backend checks: `npm --prefix backend test`.
- Follow task-specific check requirements and report skipped checks.
